package cyfr:model@0.1.0;

/// Further input for the invocation under way, which whoever started it
/// supplies while it runs: for a `model/chat@1` call, a message that
/// arrived after the call began, which the catalyst writes into its
/// harness's running session itself. Only this invocation's inputs are
/// read and reported here; a stopped, replaced or cancelled invocation
/// gets none. An error is a code: `lost`, `unavailable` or
/// `invalid_request`.
interface inputs {
    /// One input: the id its supplier knows it by, and its content, the
    /// JSON of a user message's content (a string, or `text`, `image` and
    /// `document` blocks, each attachment's data in base64).
    record input {
        id: string,
        content: string,
    }

    /// The next input not yet reported sent, or none: nobody supplies
    /// the invocation, or its supplier has none. A supplier that could not
    /// answer is `unavailable`, never none. Until it is reported, every
    /// call answers the same input: a read moves nothing.
    next: func() -> result<option<input>, string>;

    /// Report that the input `id` was handed on, once the harness accepted
    /// it. A report repeated after a lost answer marks it once; `ok` means
    /// the report was recorded.
    sent: func(id: string) -> result<_, string>;
}
